IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ny-fa`

-- New York Social Services Law Article 5 -- the family assistance applicant's questions (a parent, another relative caring
-- for a child, or a pregnant individual). Every question calls the rules in ny-fa.l4; nothing is restated here.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Can my family get family assistance`

@export Is this child young enough to count as a child for New York family assistance under Social Services Law s 349 A?
GIVEN `the child's age` IS A NUMBER @desc The child's age in whole years
      `the child is a full-time secondary school student` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the child is a full-time student regularly attending secondary school, or the equivalent level of vocational or technical training
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does this child count for family assistance` IF
    `is a child for family assistance` `the child's age` `the child is a full-time secondary school student`

@export Is my family in the group New York family assistance is given to under Social Services Law s 349?
GIVEN `I am pregnant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are pregnant
      `I am applying for a child under 18, or under 19 and a full-time secondary student` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are applying for the benefit of a child who is under 18, or under 19 and a full-time secondary or equivalent vocational student
      `the child lives with me, a parent or another adult relative` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the child lives with you, with a parent, or with another adult related to the child by blood, marriage or adoption
      `the official finds the allowance is in the child's interest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the social services official judges that granting the allowance will be in the child's interest (the official's judgment)
      `the official finds me a fit person to bring up the child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the social services official judges you a fit person to bring up the child (the official's judgment)
      `the child lived in New York on the day I applied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the child was a New York resident on the date of application
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my family in the group given family assistance` IF
    `family assistance may be given under s 349` `I am pregnant` `I am applying for a child under 18, or under 19 and a full-time secondary student` `the child lives with me, a parent or another adult relative` `the official finds the allowance is in the child's interest` `the official finds me a fit person to bring up the child` `the child lived in New York on the day I applied`

-- Only for a parent or pregnant individual under 18 and not married.
@export I am under 18 and unmarried, with a child or pregnant: does my living arrangement allow me family assistance under Social Services Law s 131(6)?
GIVEN `I am under 18 and unmarried` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are under 18 and not married
      `I care for my own child or am pregnant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you live with and care for your own child, or are pregnant
      `I live in my parent's, guardian's or adult relative's home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you live in a home kept by your parent, legal guardian or another adult relative
      `I live in an adult-supervised supportive living arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you live in an adult-supervised supportive living arrangement approved by the district (for example a second chance home or maternity home)
      `an exception applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether one of the s 131(6) exceptions applies: no parent, guardian or suitable adult relative is living or known; none will let you live with them; you or your child have been harmed or abused there; there is evidence of imminent or serious harm; or it is in your child's best interests, as determined
      `the district finds my current arrangement appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your current living arrangement is found appropriate
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my living arrangement allow me family assistance` IF
    `the minor parent rule allows family assistance for me` `I am under 18 and unmarried` `I care for my own child or am pregnant` `I live in my parent's, guardian's or adult relative's home` `I live in an adult-supervised supportive living arrangement` `an exception applies` `the district finds my current arrangement appropriate`

§ `Time limits and disqualifications`

@export Does the 60-month limit in Social Services Law s 350(2) stop my family getting TANF-funded family assistance?
GIVEN `months of assistance I have received as an adult` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months, in total and in any state, an adult in your family has received TANF-funded assistance or New York safety net cash assistance, not counting months as a child who was not the head of household or married to the head
      `the hardship exemption applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that adult is unable to work because of an independently verified physical or mental impairment (including one resulting from domestic violence), or receives SSI or additional state payments
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the sixty-month limit stop my family assistance` IF
    `the sixty-month limit bars TANF-funded family assistance` `months of assistance I have received as an adult` `the hardship exemption applies`

-- Only if you left a job or cut your hours or pay.
@export If I quit my job or cut my earnings to qualify for assistance, from what date am I no longer disqualified under Social Services Law s 131(10)?
GIVEN `the day I quit or reduced my earnings` IS A DATE @desc The day you voluntarily ended the job or reduced your earnings
GIVETH A DATE
`From when may I get assistance after quitting to qualify` MEANS
    `the first day the s 131(10) disqualification no longer applies` `the day I quit or reduced my earnings`

-- Only if a caretaker relative is in a labour dispute.
@export Does a strike stop family assistance for this month under Social Services Law s 349 D?
GIVEN `a caretaker relative the child lives with was on strike on the last day of the month` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a parent or other caretaker relative the child lives with was participating in a strike on the last day of the month
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does a strike stop family assistance this month` IF
    `the strike rule bars the month` `a caretaker relative the child lives with was on strike on the last day of the month`

§ `How much a month`

@export How much of my family's savings and property counts against family assistance under Social Services Law s 131-n(1)?
GIVEN `I already receive public assistance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are already receiving public assistance (recipients may keep more)
      `someone in my household is 60 or older or disabled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether any household member is aged 60 or over or disabled
      `my cash and other resources` IS A NUMBER @desc Cash, bank balances and other property, in US dollars, not counting your home, one car, burial plots, funeral agreements up to $1,500 each, 529 and ABLE accounts, individual development accounts, and vehicle or tuition savings accounts opened while on assistance
      `the value of my car` IS A NUMBER @desc The fair market value of one car, in US dollars; 0 if none
      `my district's car limit` IS A NUMBER @desc Your district's car value limit if it has adopted one above $12,000, in US dollars; 0 otherwise
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much of my resources counts` MEANS
    `resources not exempted by s 131-n(1)` `I already receive public assistance` `someone in my household is 60 or older or disabled` `my cash and other resources` `the value of my car` `my district's car limit`

@export What is my family's monthly standard of need under Social Services Law s 131-a(2)?
GIVEN `people in my household` IS A NUMBER @desc How many people in your household are applying or receiving assistance together
      `my shelter amount` IS A NUMBER @desc The monthly shelter amount the district allows you under the department's regulations (generally your rent up to the district's maximum), in US dollars
      `my fuel for heating amount` IS A NUMBER @desc The monthly fuel-for-heating amount the district allows you, if your heat is not included in the rent, in US dollars; 0 otherwise
      `my other allowed items` IS A NUMBER @desc Any other monthly amount the district includes for your circumstances (for example the extra cost of meals), in US dollars; 0 if none
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is my standard of need` MEANS
    `the standard of monthly need` `people in my household` `my shelter amount` `my fuel for heating amount` `my other allowed items`

@export How much of my household's monthly earnings counts against family assistance under Social Services Law s 131-a(8)?
GIVEN `monthly earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc Gross monthly earnings of the household members whose needs are counted, in US dollars (leave out the earnings of a child who is a student)
      `the earned income disregard percentage` IS A NUMBER @desc The s 131-a(8)(a)(ii) percentage in force (50% in the statute, adjusted each June by the department), as a fraction, for example 0.5
      `I quit, cut my earnings, refused a job or did not report earnings without good cause` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, without good cause, you quit or reduced your earnings or refused a job within the last 75 days, or failed to report this month's earnings in time
      `my income is above my need and I had no assistance in the last four months` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your gross income is above your standard of need and you received no public assistance in any of the four months before this one (see the next question)
      `I am in my once-in-a-lifetime six months after starting a job` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether this is one of the six months after starting a job in which, once in your life, all earnings are disregarded (total income at or below 200% of the federal poverty level)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much of my earnings counts` MEANS
    `countable earned income` `monthly earnings` `the earned income disregard percentage` `I quit, cut my earnings, refused a job or did not report earnings without good cause` `my income is above my need and I had no assistance in the last four months` `I am in my once-in-a-lifetime six months after starting a job`

@export Is my gross income above my standard of need, with no assistance in the last four months, so that I lose the $150 earnings disregard under Social Services Law s 131-a(8)(c)?
GIVEN `my gross monthly income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your household's gross monthly income before any disregard, in US dollars
      `my standard of need` IS A NUMBER @desc Your monthly standard of need (see the standard of need question), in US dollars
      `I received assistance in one of the last four months` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you received public assistance in any of the four months before the month of the decision
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I lose the 150 dollar disregard` IF
    `the s 131-a(8)(c) bar is met` `my gross monthly income` `my standard of need` `I received assistance in one of the last four months`

@export How much family assistance will my family get each month under Social Services Law s 131-a?
GIVEN `my standard of need` IS A NUMBER @desc Your monthly standard of need (see the standard of need question), in US dollars
      `my countable earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc Your countable monthly earnings (see the earnings question), in US dollars
      `child support received this month` IS A NUMBER @desc Child support paid on time for this month, in US dollars; 0 if none
      `the support is for two or more children` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that support is for two or more children
      `my other monthly income` IS A NUMBER @desc Other monthly income counted against assistance (for example unemployment benefits), in US dollars; not federal earned income credit refunds
      `my countable resources` IS A NUMBER @desc Resources that count against assistance (see the resources question), in US dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much family assistance a month` MEANS
    `the monthly grant` `my standard of need` (`my countable earnings` PLUS (`countable support payments` `child support received this month` `the support is for two or more children`) PLUS `my other monthly income`) `my countable resources`
